  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1995636 Firefox ran into a web compat issue due to `replaceState()` throwing after reaching the UA-defined limit of repeated calls. I think Gecko's current limit is 200 `replaceState`s (or `location.hash` changes; see #11410) in 10 seconds.\n\nWebKit's limit is 100. Chromium's limit is 200, but after that it [no-ops instead of throwing](https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40554715).\n\nWe're considering increasing the limit to 1000. If there's interest in aligning on the number we can codify it in the spec.",
